{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-30e0-772a-a5bc-277d5d70a561","id":"01a1a587-d66d-7726-8cc2-2f038e007c79","idempotency_key":"ae322f5389b18010148c0ae1030601a3fef6f56a888aa792434543cccb2cea76","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T07:48:25Z","payload":{"note":"crates/ai/src/reads.rs (feature host) plus crates/ai/src/result.rs. ReadHost answers position questions by replaying the board's own move list from start_fen: get_position (fen, turn, move number, halfmove clock, piece count, plies, revision, mutability), get_history (each ply with SAN and the FEN after it) and legal_moves (every legal move as sorted SAN + UCI); a board whose stored moves cannot be played is refused as internal rather than guessed at. analyze/evaluate/opening_explorer/search_database/tablebase call Engine, Openings, Games and Tablebase traits: no transport in the crate, the server injects adapters and tests inject fakes; analyze pins the engine fingerprint in the result, evaluate uses the trait's shallow default, opening_explorer reports per-move win/draw counts with the source name, search_database returns count plus samples, tablebase returns outcome/dtz/dtm/best move. Unconfigured services answer the new result_code::UNAVAILABLE with the service named, never an empty success. result.rs is now the single vocabulary for tool results (ok/applied/refused/refused_with/internal/unavailable) and board.rs uses it too. Evidence: cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features read_tools -> 13 tests (position/history/legal moves, corrupted move list refused, engine analysis with pinned fingerprint, evaluate, opening explorer, database search, tablebase, three unconfigured services, workspace counts, unknown board).","target":"t-b1ab"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
